        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void PfifoContentionTests::Initialize</definition>
        <argsstring>() override</argsstring>
        <name>Initialize</name>
        <qualifiedname>PfifoContentionTests::Initialize</qualifiedname>
        <reimplements refid="d2/d3e/classTestSuite_1a1c4756eb905d6d4d35e1630107396c38">Initialize</reimplements>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Initializes the test suite and creates test cases.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="remark"><para>Control Draws <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> tiny triangles, submitted to the GPU in a few large chunks per frame. Hits none of the targeted pathologies and serves as the baseline for the other tests.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>LongPushbuffer Draws <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> tiny triangles, submitted to the GPU all at once at the end of the frame, so the GPU processes one long uninterrupted run of commands.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>MethodChurn Draws a fixed number of tiny triangles with <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> single-DWORD state methods interleaved between them. Each method is processed individually, so the cost scales with the number of methods rather than the amount of data.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>TinyKicks Draws <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> tiny triangles, submitting each one to the GPU separately and reading a PGRAPH register from the CPU after each submission.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>HalfRatePresent Presents every other frame (30fps). The frames in between draw <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> tiny triangles to an offscreen surface without presenting, so the displayed image does not change; only those frames are recorded.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>SurfaceReadback Several times per frame, renders to an offscreen surface, queues <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> tiny triangles to the screen behind it, then reads a pixel of the offscreen surface from the CPU before queueing <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> more.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>OcclusionSpin Issues <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> zpass pixel count queries per frame, each covering a small quad, and spins on the CPU until each report has been written before issuing the next.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>CpuFramebufferWrite Draws a few tiny triangles to the back buffer, then writes <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> DWORDs directly into the back buffer from the CPU before presenting it.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="remark"><para>FillBound Draws <computeroutput>load</computeroutput> alpha blended quads covering the whole back buffer. Each quad is a handful of DWORDs but many pixels, so the frame time should be dominated by the GPU rather than by submission. Validates that the measurements can tell the two apart. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
